# Testing

## Coverage target

- Maintain **≥ 85% line coverage** on non-POJO code (services, controllers, domain logic, utilities, React components/hooks).
- **Exclude from coverage**: POJOs — DTOs, records used only as data carriers, JPA entities with no behavior, MapStruct mappers, Lombok-only types, and pure config classes.
- New or changed logic MUST not lower coverage below the threshold; add tests with the change.

## What to test

Cover **all major conditional flows**:

- Happy path and primary error paths
- Validation failures (Bean Validation and domain rules)
- Ticket **state machine**: every allowed transition, every rejected transition, edge cases
- RAG: answers cite ticket IDs, use only retrieved context, explicit response when no relevant tickets
- API layer: status codes and RFC 9457 problem responses for error cases
- Frontend: form validation, error states, loading/empty states for user-facing flows

## Backend (Java / Spring Boot)

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| Unit tests | Service logic, state machine, validators (mock dependencies) |
| `@WebMvcTest` | Controller contract, status codes, problem+json shape |
| `@DataJpaTest` | Repository queries when logic is non-trivial |
| Integration tests | Critical end-to-end paths (optional; prefer focused tests) |

- Name tests by behavior: `shouldRejectTransitionWhenTicketClosed`.
- One assertion theme per test; use clear Given/When/Then structure.
- No tests that only assert mocks were called with no behavior check.

## Frontend (React / TypeScript)

- Use **Vitest** (or project default) + React Testing Library.
- Test user-visible outcomes, not implementation details.
- Cover validation messages, disabled submit, and error display on failed API calls.

## CI & changes

- Run the full test suite before merge.
- Bug fixes MUST include a regression test when feasible.
- Do not merge with failing tests or coverage below 85% on in-scope code.
